Here is how MemoryStream is organized:
```cs
    public abstract class Stream
    {
        public void Dispose() => Close();

        public virtual void Close()
        {
            Dispose(true);
            GC.SuppressFinalize(this);
        }

        protected virtual void Dispose(bool disposing) {}
    }

    public class MemoryStream : Stream
    {
        protected override void Dispose(bool disposing)
        {
            if (disposing)
            {
                _isOpen = false;
                _writable = false;
                _expandable = false;
                _lastReadTask = default;
            }
        }
    }
```
So essentially jit can't throw Dispose away - it has to emit `GC.SuppressFinalize` and null those fields as requested.
Also, note that `MemoryStream` is not sealed so users can override it. 
We might be able to help JIT here by checking that the current object is MemoryStream (not overriden) if needed
